            <ArticleTitle>Is a tight patch necessary after trabeculectomy?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1006-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIMS" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To determine if post-trabeculectomy patching reduces the prevalence of shallow/flat anterior chambers and pain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">435 eyes were prospectively randomised to either a double patch with tape or no patch with tape group.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">There was no statistically significant difference in flat or shallow anterior chamber rates or pain symptoms between the patch and no patch groups.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">There is no benefit to patching the post-trabeculectomy eye.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
